    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
    WHEN JUST determined THEN
        IF determined THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that— (i) the Secretary may determine that extraordinary circumstances make it impracticable" (read as: the exception applies only on that determination)

-- src:1538 | (ii) a State agency that obtains in­formation collected under section 1611(e)(1)(I)(i)(I) of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1382(e)(1)(I)(i)(I)) pursuant to section 1611(e)(1)(I)(ii)(II) of that Act (42 U.S.C. 1382(e)(1)(I)(ii)(II)), or under another program determined by the Secretary to be comparable to the program carried out under that section, shall be considered in compliance with this subparagraph.
-- jural: the State agency | the Secretary | immunity: a State agency using the Social Security Act information or a comparable program's is considered in compliance
@ref s 2020(e)(18)(B)(ii) (src:1538)
